[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-sim-substrate-scoring-260526", :doc/title "Sim Substrate Scoring Evidence — ADR-2605261600 companion", :doc/status "r0-preflight-evidence", :doc/doc_type "evidence", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/body "\n# Sim Substrate Scoring Evidence — ADR-2605261600 companion\n\nThis document is the **R0 scoring evidence skeleton** explicitly reserved by\nADR-2605261600 §R0 (\"`90-docs/baien/sim-substrate-scoring-260526.edn` (R0\nscaffold; per-dimension methodology + per-actor pilot run logs land here R1+)\").\n\nIt records the first pass at: **does the OSS stack mandated by ADR-2605261600\nactually function on a developer machine?** Evidence below is generated by the\npreflight harness at `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/`.\n\n## Pass / fail at a glance\n\n| # | Dimension | Tool | Pass? | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | G7 same-hw bit-identical replay | MuJoCo 3.8.1 | ✅ | sha256 match across 5000 steps, max diff = 0 |\n| 2 | Articulated physics (CPU) | MuJoCo MJX 3.8.1 | ✅ | 16× JIT parallel rollout; chassis-position diff vs C++ ~1e-4 m |\n| 3 | Forward photoreal render | Mitsuba 3.8.0 (`scalar_rgb`) | ✅ | `kusawake_render.png` (640×480, ~400 KB) |\n| 4 | Differentiable rendering | Mitsuba 3.8.0 (`llvm_ad_rgb`, PRB) | ✅ | BSDF reflectance optimization, loss 0.00258 → 0.00059 over 8 iter |\n| 5 | Scene composition (text + binary) | OpenUSD 26.5 (`usd-core`) | ✅ | `.usda` → `.usdc` (78% size) → reference-based 4-instance fleet |\n| 6 | Geometric raycast lidar proxy | MuJoCo `mj_ray` | ✅ | 5760 rays → 2520 hits; correct geom histogram (ground / vine / chassis / wheel) |\n\nAll evidence files committed under `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/out/`.\n\n## Environment (where this evidence was generated)\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Hardware | Apple Silicon Mac, arm64 |\n| OS | macOS Darwin 25.3.0 |\n| Python | 3.12.13 (Homebrew) |\n| MuJoCo | 3.8.1 |\n| mujoco-mjx | 3.8.1 |\n| JAX | 0.10.1, backend = cpu |\n| Mitsuba | 3.8.0 |\n| drjit | 1.3.1 |\n| usd-core | 26.5 |\n| libLLVM | Homebrew `llvm` (libLLVM-22) at `/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/libLLVM.dylib` |\n\n## Findings that should propagate into R1 ADRs\n\nThese are concrete constraints discovered through preflight that R1 ADR\ndrafters need to encode:\n\n1. **libLLVM is a build-time dependency for Mitsuba 3 differentiable rendering.**\n   Even `scalar_rgb` variant fails without `libLLVM.dylib` reachable via\n   `DRJIT_LIBLLVM_PATH`. The R1 ADR for Kusawake (or any actor binding R1\n   sim) must include libLLVM provisioning in the Murakumo node setup. This\n   is compatible with G1 (`brew install llvm` is Apache-2.0).\n\n2. **MuJoCo MJX has unimplemented geom-pair collisions** (notably\n   `cylinder × box`). Workaround: use `capsule` for wheel geometry in any\n   MJCF intended to run under MJX. Two MJCF variants now exist:\n   `kusawake.xml` (cylinder wheels — C++ MuJoCo + interactive viewer) and\n   `kusawake_mjx.xml` (capsule wheels — MJX-compatible). R1 ADR should\n   either (a) standardize on capsule wheels for MJX-bound actors, or\n   (b) gate MJX use on a per-actor geometry audit.\n\n3. **JAX CPU is slower than MuJoCo C++ at small batch sizes.** On Apple\n   Silicon, 16× parallel MJX rollout on CPU takes ~20 ms/rollout vs C++\n   2.3 ms/rollout (0.1× speedup). The GPU/TPU advantage of MJX only shows\n   up on accelerator devices. R1 ADR should bind MJX execution to Murakumo\n   EVO-X2 ROCm (per ADR-2605215000) and measure the speedup target there\n   before claiming MJX wins on Apple Silicon developer machines.\n\n4. **PRB (Path Replay Backprop) supports BSDF gradients, not emitter\n   position.** Attempting to optimize a point-light position via PRB\n   triggers \"contribution is not attached to the AD graph\" because\n   light-position derivatives are discontinuous (direct visibility). R1\n   G5 measurement strategy should specify BSDF reflectance / scale /\n   geometry parameters as the differentiable parameter, not light pose.\n\n5. **`mj_ray` lidar proxy is single-threaded loop in Python**, ~5760 rays\n   in <1s but not scalable. R2 binding to CARLA lidar kernel + Vulkan RT\n   stays mandatory. The proxy validates the geometry pipeline only.\n\n6. **USD references work cleanly for fleet composition.** A 4-instance\n   `kusawake_fleet.usda` is 982 bytes (vs ~12 KB if each instance were\n   expanded). R3 community-scale (≤30 units) fleet definitions should\n   adopt USD reference graph from the start.\n\n## Dimensions deliberately not exercised at preflight\n\nThese need the R1+ Murakumo-fleet binding before they can land:\n\n- **G4 Murakumo fleet execution** — preflight runs on dev Mac, not fleet\n- **G5 ≥ 0.75 vs Isaac Sim ground truth** — requires the isolated trial\n  machine per ADR-2605261600 §G5 carve-out (one-time-use, decommissioned)\n- **G6 `simulationRunAttestation` lexicon emission** — schema is R1 work\n- **G7 cross-hardware bit-identical replay** — preflight covers same-hw only\n- **G8 NVIDIA-account-required runtime tools** — vacuously true (we use none)\n- **G10 Charter Rider §2 asset scan** — vacuously true (only primitive cubes\n  and cylinders used; no asset-marketplace imports)\n- **G11 simToRealHandoverAttestation** — requires R1 real-robot pilot\n- **G13 telemetry-free build** — verified by inspection (no telemetry imports);\n  formal compile-time disable lands at R1\n- **Vulkan RT** — Apple Silicon is not a Vulkan RT platform; R2 EVO-X2 territory\n- **HdCycles** — R1 binding; this harness uses Mitsuba 3 standalone\n\n## R1 entrance criteria (updated from preflight)\n\nADR-2605261600 §R1 lists \"HdCycles + Mitsuba 3 + Embree differential PoC +\nfirst eligible R1 consumer = igata R1 (ADR-2605261215) static die surface\nrender\". Preflight evidence does not change this binding but adds these\nconcrete prerequisites:\n\n| Prerequisite | Where it must be specified |\n|---|---|\n| libLLVM in Murakumo node setup | R1 actor ADR §Environment |\n| MJX-compatible MJCF (capsule wheels) | R1 actor ADR §Geometry |\n| Differentiable parameter = BSDF, not pose | R1 G5 measurement strategy |\n| MJX speedup measured on EVO-X2 ROCm | R1 acceptance criteria |\n| Cross-hw replay test (G7 R1 deliverable) | R1 actor ADR §Reproducibility |\n\n## Companion file index\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/README.edn` | Harness usage + scope vs operational |\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/pyproject.toml` | Reproducible Python deps |\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/kusawake.xml` | Reference MJCF (cylinder wheels) |\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/kusawake_mjx.xml` | MJX-compatible MJCF (capsule wheels) |\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/verify_*.py` | 6 evidence scripts |\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/view.py` | Native MuJoCo interactive viewer |\n| `70-tools/e7m-sim-preflight/out/` | Generated artifacts (PNG, USD, PLY) |\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605261600 — Robotics Simulation Substrate R0 Charter\n- ADR-2605252615 — Kusawake (草分け) Autonomous Agri-Mobile Platform R0\n- ADR-2605215000 — Etzhayyim Inference Murakumo-Only (no commercial GPU rental)\n- ADR-2605191524 — Witness Quorum + Transparent Force Swarm Broadcast\n- ADR-2605242630 — Baien R1a WebGPU LoRA backward-pass PoC (precedent for\n  \"R0/R1 scaffolding + sha256-pinned evidence committed to repo\")\n", :doc/path "90-docs/baien/sim-substrate-scoring-260526.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-25", :doc/date "2026-05-25", :doc/authoritative_for ["ADR-2605261600 §R0 \"scoring evidence skeleton\" deliverable" "ADR-2605252615 §R0 \"MuJoCo + Mitsuba 3 + USD + mj_ray preflight"]}]
